WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.292 --> 00:00:01.251
The world I knew

00:00:01.251 --> 00:00:02.211
was quite simple.

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:03.962
I didn't know

00:00:03.962 --> 00:00:05.839
there was such a
thing as electricity.

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:07.132
Or that water could

00:00:07.132 --> 00:00:09.134
come into the house
through a pipe.

00:00:09.426 --> 00:00:11.220
I never thought about
what I looked like.

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:14.056
I didn't know what a mirror was!

00:00:14.431 --> 00:00:16.016
♪♪

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:17.351
When you grow up
in a community

00:00:17.351 --> 00:00:18.727
where everything you know

00:00:18.727 --> 00:00:20.062
is powerful and good

00:00:20.062 --> 00:00:21.647
and it's black,

00:00:21.647 --> 00:00:23.482
there's no concept of race.

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:25.484
That defines Sidney Poitier.

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:29.029
I left The Bahamas with
this sense of myself.

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:30.864
And from the time
I got off the boat,

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:33.116
America began to say to me,

00:00:33.534 --> 00:00:34.660
"You're not who
you think you are."

00:00:35.285 --> 00:00:36.703
♪♪

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.538
There was a habit in Hollywood

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:40.290
of utilizing blacks

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:42.292
in the most
disrespectful ways.

00:00:42.292 --> 00:00:44.419
I said, "I cannot play that."

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:45.921
I don't think Sidney ever

00:00:45.921 --> 00:00:47.965
played a subservient part.

00:00:48.465 --> 00:00:49.883
Never bucked his eyes,

00:00:49.925 --> 00:00:51.301
never ducked his head.

00:00:51.301 --> 00:00:53.887
They call me, Mister Tibbs.

00:00:55.222 --> 00:00:55.973
Yeah!

00:00:55.973 --> 00:00:58.475
♪♪

00:00:58.475 --> 00:00:59.977
It was the first time I've

00:00:59.977 --> 00:01:02.688
seen a black man
assert his power.

00:01:02.688 --> 00:01:03.689
I'm a giant

00:01:03.689 --> 00:01:04.940
and I'm surrounded by ants.

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:06.900
I wanted to marry
Sidney Poitier.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.527
He was like, wow!

00:01:08.527 --> 00:01:09.945
Movie stars
should be...

00:01:09.945 --> 00:01:11.154
wow.

00:01:11.154 --> 00:01:12.531
Biggest box office draw

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:15.909
Black Man 1967-68'.

00:01:16.868 --> 00:01:19.997
And the whole
country is spiraling

00:01:20.455 --> 00:01:21.290
around him.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:25.002
We're hanging together by

00:01:25.002 --> 00:01:26.712
a few cultural threads.

00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:28.213
And Sidney Poitier

00:01:28.213 --> 00:01:30.007
is one of those
cultural threads.

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:32.342
The winner is Sidney Poitier.

00:01:33.719 --> 00:01:35.512
And it's not easy
being the first

00:01:35.512 --> 00:01:37.097
when you have to

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:39.933
represent the entire race.

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:42.102
♪♪

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:43.103
He had big shoulders-

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:44.271
he was given big shoulders,

00:01:44.271 --> 00:01:45.522
but he had to carry
a lot of weight.

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:47.941
If there were equality of
opportunity

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:49.109
in this business,

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:50.110
there'd be 15

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:51.611
Sidney Poitier's and 10 or 12

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:52.529
Bellafonte’s.

00:01:52.529 --> 00:01:54.323
But there is not.
-Probably other way around.

00:01:54.323 --> 00:01:55.949
Watch it, watch it,
watch it.

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:56.992
[laughs]

00:01:57.492 --> 00:01:58.744
He was gonna put black people

00:01:58.744 --> 00:02:00.954
in positions where
they can have a career

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:02.289
behind the camera.

00:02:02.539 --> 00:02:04.124
He came to this Earth

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:05.250
to move it,

00:02:05.334 --> 00:02:06.293
to change it,

00:02:06.335 --> 00:02:07.419
to shake it.

00:02:07.419 --> 00:02:08.545
You think of yourself

00:02:08.545 --> 00:02:10.213
as a colored man,

00:02:10.213 --> 00:02:12.215
I think of myself as a man.

00:02:13.467 --> 00:02:14.760
♪♪

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:15.969
That's the summary of him.

00:02:16.386 --> 00:02:17.971
I love him so much.

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:21.058
My life had
more than a few

00:02:21.058 --> 00:02:23.602
wonderful,
indescribable turns.

00:02:23.894 --> 00:02:26.897
♪♪

00:02:29.524 --> 00:02:31.401
And I have lived them.

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:35.572
♪♪

